{#- A "hot" item: a chart, bar, ring, tile or row that shows its readout when pointed at or
    keyboard-focused, and in the app opens its bigger view. Imported with context: it uses
    `mode` and `open_link`. The readout is plain text from readouts.py, escaped like any other.

    In the app the item is a tearsheet://open link. A file has no app to open anything, so the
    item is focusable on its own (tabindex 0) and keeps its readout. A view the app doesn't know
    gives no link, and the item is then focusable the same way. An empty readout (nothing stored
    to say) leaves out the readout and the label, and the item is named by what it holds. -#}
{%- macro hot(view, item, text, cls="") -%}
{%- set link = open_link(view, item) if mode == "app" else none -%}
<a class="hot{% if cls %} {{ cls }}{% endif %}"{% if link %} href="{{ link }}"{% else %} tabindex="0" role="group"{% endif %}{% if text %} aria-label="{{ text }}"{% endif %}>{{ caller() }}{% if text %}<span class="ro" aria-hidden="true">{{ text }}</span>{% endif %}</a>
{%- endmacro -%}
